# Determines the superclass reference of pClassRef.
# The $superclass attribute can be of the form MyClass or MyLib.MyClass.
# Resolution is done by the CORE (undocumented, reverse engineered from
# IDE shell oLibraries.$cmenuclick Case 30, Superclass methods):
#   $dotoolmethod(kEnvToolBrowser,185,libRef,superclassString) Returns superRef
# The core resolves both forms, cross-library, incl. locked classes.
# Returns the superclass itemref, or NULL if the class has no superclass.
# Related: 208 = modal set-superclass dialog (libRef,className,outName)
# Returns selected. The dialog only PICKS, the caller must assign:
#   Calculate libRef.$classes.[name].$superclass as outName
Calculate superclassName as pClassRef.$superclass
If len(superclassName)=0
	Quit method classRef.$ref
End If
Do $root.$modes.$dotoolmethod(kEnvToolBrowser,185,pClassRef.$lib().$ref,superclassName) Returns classRef ## @CORE
Quit method classRef.$ref